# No dead scaffolding

Do not add a dependency, a config, an abstraction layer, or a "we'll need this
later" export.

- No option nobody passes.
- No interface with one implementer added "for testing".
- No helper exported because it might be useful.
- No reserved vocabulary word implemented early — `VOCAB.md` names six that are
  reserved, and each arrives with its own card, its tests and its lint.

The cheapest code to maintain is the code you did not write; the second
cheapest is the code you deleted when its card turned out not to need it.

*(A local rule, beyond the eight in `.llm/rules/`. It has never conflicted with
them.)*
